// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO4/5 (touch RST/INT), GPIO7/8 (dedicated
// onboard I2C), GPIO9-13 (I2S audio), GPIO22/23 (LCD backlight/reset),
// GPIO45 (SDMMC power), GPIO53 (audio amp ctrl) - see vendor
// pins_arduino.h.
// INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED (2026-07-14) for most pins via 4D Systems'
// own ESP32-P4 Round Series resource-centre datasheet content (surfaced
// via search - the PDF/HTML itself blocks direct fetch, 403): the round
// display uses a Goodix GT967 capacitive touch controller (vs GT928 on
// the rectangular sibling) on the same I2C bus GPIO7/8; LCD is a JD9365
// MIPI panel with reset on GPIO23 and a Silergy SY7023 backlight driver
// on GPIO22; I2S audio (GPIO9-13) plus the same I2C bus (7/8) drive an
// ES8311 codec, with an NSIWay NS4150B Class-D amp downstream of the
// codec (consistent with AMP_CTRL=53). This board.json is confirmed
// byte-identical to its rectangular sibling esp32p4_4ds_mipi's board.json
// (same 4D Systems ESP32-P4 MIPI carrier board design; only the touch
// controller IC and glass shape differ, not the GPIO wiring). GPIO4/5
// (CTP_RST/CTP_INT) and the specific GPIO45 SDMMC-power role were NOT
// independently confirmed beyond this board's own pins_arduino.h naming -
// see boardsDetails notes.txt. Left excluded (no change) as the
// conservative/safe direction.
